{"name":"Columbine","hex":"#f5dae3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Columbine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A census-designated place in Arapahoe County and Jefferson County, Colorado, United States.","The sweetheart of Harlequin in old pantomimes."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An incident in which someone shoots multiple people at a school."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Columbine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Columbine, Colorado","blocks":[{"text":"Columbine is a census-designated place (CDP) in and governed by Jefferson and Arapahoe counties in Colorado, United States. The CDP is a part of the Denver metropolitan area. Located primarily in Jefferson County, Columbine lies immediately south of Denver. The population of the Columbine CDP was 25,229 at the 2020 census. The community lies in ZIP code 80123."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Jefferson_County_Colorado_Incorporated_and_Unincorporated_areas_Columbine_Highlighted.svg/330px-Jefferson_County_Colorado_Incorporated_and_Unincorporated_areas_Columbine_Highlighted.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Columbine%2C_Colorado"},{"title":"Columbine High School","blocks":[{"text":"Columbine High School (CHS) is a public high school in Columbine, Colorado, United States. It is part of Jefferson County Public Schools. In the 2024–25 academic year, it enrolled 1,710 students."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Columbine_High_School_sign.jpg/330px-Columbine_High_School_sign.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Columbine_High_School"},{"title":"Columbine (stock character)","blocks":[{"text":"Columbine is a stock character in the commedia dell'arte. She is Harlequin's mistress, a comic servant playing the tricky slave type, and love interest of Pierrot. Rudlin and Crick use the Italian spelling Colombina in Commedia dell'Arte: A Handbook for Troupes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/SAND_Maurice_Masques_et_bouffons_03.jpg/330px-SAND_Maurice_Masques_et_bouffons_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Columbine_(stock_character)"},{"title":"Columbine (book)","blocks":[{"text":"Columbine is a non-fiction book written by Dave Cullen and published by Twelve on April 6, 2009. It is an examination of the Columbine High School massacre, on April 20, 1999, and the perpetrators Eric Harris and Dylan Klebold. The book covers two major storylines: the killers' lives leading up to the attack, and the survivors' struggles with the aftermath over the following decade. Chapters alternate between the two stories. Graphic depictions of parts of the attack are included, in addition to the actual names of friends and family."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/92/Columbinebookcover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Columbine_(book)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Hope_Columbine_Memorial_Library.jpg/500px-Hope_Columbine_Memorial_Library.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Hope_Columbine_Memorial_Library.jpg/1280px-Hope_Columbine_Memorial_Library.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Hope_Columbine_Memorial_Library.jpg/500px-Hope_Columbine_Memorial_Library.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHope_Columbine_Memorial_Library.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c